Package: watcher-capture
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: record a shell session for The Watcher's graded debrief
 watcher-capture records the commands you run against a target - every command,
 its output and the gaps between them - by driving your shell through a userspace
 PTY (openpty on Unix). It uses no eBPF, ptrace or kernel hooks, and needs no
 root.
 .
 The capture becomes a graded debrief in The Watcher: a per-phase audit across
 MITRE ATT&CK, the Unified Kill Chain and CWE. It streams into the running app
 live, or writes a session file for later import. Processing is deterministic and
 happens on your machine; nothing is uploaded.
